{"id":28791,"slug":"a-touch-of-zen","title":"A Touch of Zen","year":1971,"country":"Taiwan","duration":180,"spine":825,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28791-a-touch-of-zen","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/58e3f9ca227dd46e198b81b8a03229a0/nzrMRtpgt0wCrxI2HNwKb1d1XGi93S_large.jpg","description":"“Visionary” barely begins to describe this masterpiece of Chinese cinema and martial arts moviemaking. A Touch of Zen (Xia nu) by King Hu depicts the journey of Yang, a fugitive noblewoman in disguise who seeks refuge in a remote, and allegedly haunted, village. The sanctuary she and her three companions find with a shy scholar is shattered when a nefarious swordsman uncovers her identity, pitting the five against legions of blade-wielding opponents. At once a wuxia film, the tale of a spiritual quest, and a study in human nature, A Touch of Zen is an unparalleled work in Hu’s formidable career and an epic of the highest order, characterized by breathtaking action choreography, stunning widescreen landscapes, and innovative editing.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"King Hu","slug":"king-hu"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Hsu Feng","role":"Yang Hui-zhen","slug":"hsu-feng"},{"actor":"Shih Chun","role":"Gu Sheng-zhai","slug":"shih-chun"},{"actor":"Bai Ying","role":"General Shi Wen-qiao","slug":"bai-ying"},{"actor":"Xue Han","role":"General Lu Ding-an","slug":"xue-han"},{"actor":"Zhang Bing-yu","role":"Gu’s mother","slug":"zhang-bing-yu"},{"actor":"Cao Jian","role":"Xu Zheng-qing","slug":"cao-jian"},{"actor":"Jia Lu-shi","role":"Yang Lian","slug":"jia-lu-shi"},{"actor":"Wan Zhong-shan","role":"Lu Qiang","slug":"wan-zhong-shan"},{"actor":"Tien Peng","role":"Ouyang Nian","slug":"tien-peng"},{"actor":"Wang Rui","role":"Men Da","slug":"wang-rui"},{"actor":"Han Ying-jie","role":"Xu Xian-chun","slug":"han-ying-jie"},{"actor":"Miao Tian","role":"Nie Qiu","slug":"miao-tian"},{"actor":"Roy Chiao","role":"Abbot Hui-yuan","slug":"roy-chiao"}],"credits":[